    [Not used in road design standards.],
    [ISO 6976 / German RASt: transition curves between circular arcs are specified as clothoids @wild2010. The model matches real road geometry by construction.],
  ),
  caption: [Clothoids vs. Bézier curves for vehicle trajectory representation.],
)

In summary: Bézier curves are optimal for rendering and shape design. Clothoids
are optimal when the curve must be *physically interpretable*, *dynamically
analysable*, and *compatible with road geometry standards* — all of which apply
here.

